  "id": "uz2x3v1",
  "title": "Chapter 6: Computer Memory",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cmhudtc",
      "content": "Computer memory is the storage area in a computer where data, instructions, and results are stored. It plays a crucial role in computer functioning because all processing requires data and instructions to be stored in memory. Computer memory is broadly classified into Primary Memory and Secondary Memory."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Primary Storage",
          "value": "RAM & ROM",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
