    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qm8xgif",
      "content": "Cache memory is a high-speed memory located close to the CPU. It stores frequently used instructions to speed up processing."
    },
    {
      "id": "jcqd25x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.2 Secondary Memory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xc1i3sh",
      "content": "Secondary memory is used for long-term storage of data and programs. It is non-volatile and retains data even when power is turned off."
    },
